frankensim-shell-assembly-options-v1
# The same il Cannone h8 geometry and modern O1 exterior film as
# cannone-h8-varnished.assembly, with complete passive material histories.
# This is a modern measured oil/copal surrogate, not a historical recipe.
window-hz 15 2000
projection-work 549755813888
reference-thickness-m 0.003
pack spruce @body
pack maple violin-maple-sycamore-sonderegger2013-shell.fsmatpk
# Explicit modeling choice: fit sixteen candidate positive Prony arms, require
# sampled storage and loss errors below 0.1%, and reserve at most 512 histories
# after equal-time aggregation over the whole assembled body. This is a cap,
# not a promise that all 512 fit the separate prepared resources. O1 retains 13
# positive times: at 30 body modes there are at most 390 histories, which fit
# the original 4 GiB / 1e15-work declaration; the full 512 case would refuse.
# The source fit
# remains finite-band; causal continuation outside it is an authored model.
# Use the existing cannone-dominant-g3.material-strings prepared resources.
coating-memory prony-continuation 16 0.001 0.001 512
# Identical thickness, source, side, reference and tensor assumptions to the
# frozen-film recipe. The final storage-drift field belongs to frozen mode;
# hereditary mode uses the separately declared fit tolerances above.
coating @exterior varnish-oil-copal-lammlein2021-s1.fsmatpk positive 0.000020 1000 0.30 0.001 0.35 0.25
bridge-component bridge
bridge-direction 1 0 0
bridge -0.01734 -0.05164
bridge -0.00557 -0.05421
bridge 0.00629 -0.05329
bridge 0.01728 -0.04887
